(LumiCity Run Guide) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Overview) Tj
T*
(LumiCity is a Streamlit application for smart street light monitoring, prediction,) Tj
T*
(camera-based traffic response, and light intensity analysis. This project folder also) Tj
T*
(includes a Jupyter notebook used for the model-building and analysis workflow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Files to copy to another device) Tj
T*
(Copy the full project folder so these files stay together: app.py, credentials.json,) Tj
T*
(kerala_smart_lights.db, intensity_model.pkl, intensity_scaler.pkl, yolov8n.pt,) Tj
T*
(requirements.txt, requirement.txt, and LumiCity_Step_by_Step_Analysis.ipynb if you want) Tj
T*
(the notebook too.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(System requirements) Tj
T*
(Windows is the safest target because the app uses cv2.CAP_DSHOW for camera access.) Tj
T*
(Install Python 3.10 to 3.13 and make sure pip is available. A webcam is only needed for) Tj
T*
(the Camera Surveillance tab.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Environment setup) Tj
T*
(1. Open a terminal inside the project folder.) Tj
T*
(2. Create a virtual environment: python -m venv .venv) Tj
T*
(3. Activate it on PowerShell: .venv\\Scripts\\Activate.ps1) Tj
T*
(4. Upgrade pip: python -m pip install --upgrade pip) Tj
T*
(5. Install dependencies: pip install -r requirements.txt) Tj
T*
(   You can also use requirement.txt because it contains the same package list.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Run the application) Tj
T*
(Start the app with: streamlit run app.py) Tj
T*
(After Streamlit starts, open the local URL shown in the terminal, usually) Tj
T*
(http://localhost:8501.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(What the app depends on at runtime) Tj
T*
(The app expects the SQLite database, model pickle files, YOLO weights file, and) Tj
T*
(credentials.json to be present in the same folder as app.py. If any of these are) Tj
T*
(missing, some features will fail or show empty data.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Internet access) Tj
T*
(Live weather and NASA VIIRS retrieval need internet access. If those services are) Tj
T*
(unavailable, the app may fall back to defaults or show stale data depending on the) Tj
T*
(workflow.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Notebook usage) Tj
T*
(If you want to open LumiCity_Step_by_Step_Analysis.ipynb, run: jupyter notebook or open) Tj
T*
(the notebook in VS Code after installing the same requirements. The notebook includes) Tj
T*
ET
